  "description": "Major-key funk at 104 bpm, the groove on the sixteenths with a light swing (0.12): an E9 vamp with an A9 move and a B7 turnaround, a chorus walking up through C#m7 and F#m7. Techniques to copy: ghost-note snares (o) around a backbeat accent (X), a kick that pushes off the beat instead of four on the floor, a sixteenth bassline written as notes (the root, its push, an octave pop, the flat seventh, a pickup) that changes shape every other bar, a clavinet comping only the off-sixteenths, brass stabs on the chorus hits, a drum fill and a crash at each phrase end, and a breakdown where the clav and brass drop out and the bass carries the groove alone.",
